And Nikaido's passionate commentary.

146
00:09:30,628 --> 00:09:32,988
Did you take those impassioned words of his to heart?

147
00:09:33,148 --> 00:09:35,208
Boy, you gotta admit, he really gave it up.

148
00:09:35,468 --> 00:09:37,768
Friendship truly is a wonderful thing, isn't it?

149
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:41,248
Wow, just thinking about it again really pulls on the old heartstrings.

150
00:09:41,688 --> 00:09:44,948
We happened to be at our teacher's birthday party the day it aired.

151
00:09:45,308 --> 00:09:47,768
We all watched the recording together that night.

152
00:09:48,228 --> 00:09:50,348
If you really want to win, stick it out!

153
00:09:50,468 --> 00:09:52,108
Don't just attack, you've got to defend!

154
00:09:53,448 --> 00:09:56,588
Oh no, my eyes are watering.

155
00:09:56,588 --> 00:09:58,528
Oh, I think I'm crying.

156
00:09:58,768 --> 00:10:00,048
What a good kid.

157
00:10:00,568 --> 00:10:01,788
I can't believe this.

158
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:03,348
I feel so sentimental.

159
00:10:03,748 --> 00:10:06,208
The slightest thing makes me tear up these days.

160
00:10:06,508 --> 00:10:09,628
Ah, Nikaido, you're one of the few good ones.

161
00:10:09,668 --> 00:10:14,448
I'm telling you, his sincerity and passion had a room full of adults bawling like little babies.

162
00:10:15,288 --> 00:10:17,008
That broadcast really drained him.

163
00:10:17,448 --> 00:10:20,968
I heard he had a bout of anemia later and was so ill he couldn't get to his feet.

164
00:10:21,368 --> 00:10:22,808
Huh? No way.

165
00:10:23,408 --> 00:10:26,008
He must have used a lot of energy on that rant.

166
00:10:26,588 --> 00:10:28,068
He gave it everything he had.

167
00:10:29,168 --> 00:10:30,968
Right, Kiriyama?

168
00:10:31,428 --> 00:10:31,928
Right?

169
00:10:34,468 --> 00:10:38,048
Everything that guy does is for you, but none of it reaches your heart.

170
00:10:38,128 --> 00:10:39,148
It's so frustrating!

171
00:10:39,928 --> 00:10:42,888
Nikaido has six wins, and he's incredibly focused.

172
00:10:43,228 --> 00:10:45,228
He'll probably get promoted this season.

173
00:10:45,488 --> 00:10:49,268
Right now, his head is filled with the thought of facing off against you in C1.

174
00:10:49,268 --> 00:10:50,888
Come on, Kiriyama!

175
00:10:51,148 --> 00:10:53,148
You can't disappoint your friend Nikaido!

176
00:10:53,148 --> 00:11:01,608
Three wins and three losses.

177
00:11:02,068 --> 00:11:03,508
I can't lose another match.

178
00:11:03,908 --> 00:11:06,328
If I do, I'll get a degradation point.

179
00:11:06,888 --> 00:11:12,248
If that happens, a player can't regain ground and needs more wins than losses the next season.

180
00:11:12,248 --> 00:11:15,648
If you get two degradation points, you drop down one class.

181
00:11:17,528 --> 00:11:20,368
It's not easy to recover from a setback like that.

182
00:11:20,928 --> 00:11:24,048
It then takes much more effort to continue moving forward.

183
00:11:24,048 --> 00:11:28,628
I should know.

184
00:11:28,628 --> 00:11:32,088
I watched as my adoptive father went through that struggle.

185
00:11:32,728 --> 00:11:34,268
He seesawed in ranks for years.

186
00:11:34,888 --> 00:11:37,168
It was all after he was downgraded from B1.

187
00:11:37,908 --> 00:11:40,008
And it was painful to witness.

188
00:11:44,848 --> 00:11:46,788
Play your own style of show game!

189
00:11:46,948 --> 00:11:49,408
You're better than this and you know it, Kiriyama!

190
00:11:49,408 --> 00:11:53,708
I don't know how Nikaido has that much energy.

191
00:11:54,568 --> 00:11:56,908
He's obviously not a very healthy guy.

192
00:11:58,088 --> 00:12:00,188
Is it because he never doubts himself?

193
00:12:01,268 --> 00:12:04,648
His passion and determination always seems to drive him on.

194
00:12:08,088 --> 00:12:11,008
It makes me feel like I'm lagging behind somehow.

195
00:12:12,588 --> 00:12:17,648
And because of that, I can't help but feeling even worse about myself.

196
00:12:19,408 --> 00:12:26,368
He did a great job drawing it.

197
00:12:26,608 --> 00:12:27,828
He's so talented.

198
00:12:30,528 --> 00:12:33,448
Sounds like Hina and Momo really enjoyed the lesson.

199
00:12:38,088 --> 00:12:40,848
My paw pants is gonna not do silly!

200
00:12:42,568 --> 00:12:43,868
Momo, stop that!

201
00:12:44,028 --> 00:12:45,228
The kitty doesn't like it!

202
00:12:45,228 --> 00:12:49,708
They even put copies of the picture book up on the fridge so they can remember the moves.

203
00:12:53,068 --> 00:12:54,528
Grandpa is impressed too.

204
00:12:55,468 --> 00:12:56,508
Man, they're lucky!

205
00:12:57,228 --> 00:13:01,388
I hope they realize what an opportunity they've got being tutored by those two pros.

206
00:13:01,788 --> 00:13:05,148
Maybe they'll keep playing and become skilled professionals themselves.

207
00:13:05,528 --> 00:13:07,568
But I can't let them beat me, can I?

208
00:13:07,568 --> 00:13:11,188
I only wish that those two guys would tutor me as well.

209
00:13:11,368 --> 00:13:12,828
What's this world coming to?

210
00:13:13,228 --> 00:13:14,028
It's cute!

211
00:13:14,688 --> 00:13:17,528
Now he can't wait to play Shogi with his granddaughters.

212
00:13:21,308 --> 00:13:24,648
When I start to think about it like that, Shogi is pretty great.

213
00:13:25,628 --> 00:13:31,948
It's been around for hundreds of years, and even now, if you have the board in pieces, you can still enjoy it at home.

214
00:13:31,948 --> 00:13:34,088
And anyone can learn how to play it.

215
00:13:34,268 --> 00:13:36,468
It doesn't matter if you're a child or an adult.

216
00:13:36,828 --> 00:13:38,908
It's the type of game that anyone can enjoy.

217
00:13:39,488 --> 00:13:40,808
And it never gets old.

218
00:13:41,188 --> 00:13:42,508
It's a wonderful game.

219
00:13:42,968 --> 00:13:44,508
Ah! The kitty transformed!

220
00:13:46,508 --> 00:13:48,928
Memories of my dad kept coming up in my mind.

221
00:13:49,308 --> 00:13:50,788
I could see him so clearly.

222
00:13:51,788 --> 00:13:56,248
He'd gently rock back and forth, arms folded with his left hand on his cheek.

223
00:13:56,248 --> 00:13:59,668
It happened whenever he was really focusing on something.

224
00:14:00,788 --> 00:14:02,688
I liked watching him when he was like that.

225
00:14:03,728 --> 00:14:04,908
But it was rare.

226
00:14:05,668 --> 00:14:09,348
If I studied hard enough and played well, he'd get absorbed in the game.

227
00:14:10,868 --> 00:14:13,648
So I did all that I could for that look.

228
00:14:14,848 --> 00:14:19,428
He was kind and considerate of those around him, always smiling.

229
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:22,268
That's when he was his true self.

230
00:14:22,268 --> 00:14:28,508
I wonder, what would my dad think if he saw me now?

231
00:14:31,008 --> 00:14:31,888
That's right.

232
00:14:35,628 --> 00:14:36,188
Wow.

233
00:14:36,628 --> 00:14:38,248
How could I have forgotten that?

234
00:14:39,188 --> 00:14:40,108
Right now.

235
00:14:40,868 --> 00:14:43,228
I'm exactly where my dad always longed to be.

236
00:14:44,048 --> 00:14:45,768
In his world of Shogi.

237
00:14:45,768 --> 00:14:52,308
But how?

238
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,648
How could I have forgotten?

239
00:14:56,868 --> 00:14:58,388
When it's so important.

240
00:15:15,768 --> 00:15:27,908
Hi, Kyoko.

241
00:15:27,908 --> 00:15:33,188
Long time no see, Rei.

242
00:15:33,188 --> 00:15:46,888
Once when I was little, I saw lightning strike on a clear day.

243
00:15:47,848 --> 00:15:52,948
It was like a fleeting streak of liquid silver, rolling across the blue sky.

244
00:15:55,028 --> 00:15:58,148
That moment captivated me completely.

245
00:15:59,248 --> 00:16:01,208
It was an elusive flash of light.

246
00:16:01,208 --> 00:16:10,108
But inevitably, it would be followed by a driving downpour of rain.

247
00:16:12,588 --> 00:16:13,788
You're looking well.

248
00:16:16,008 --> 00:16:17,908
So why are you here?

249
00:16:18,548 --> 00:16:19,468
What do you mean?

250
00:16:19,808 --> 00:16:21,288
What kind of question is that?

251
00:16:21,908 --> 00:16:25,868
What's wrong with a big sister worrying about her little brother now that he's living all alone?

252
00:16:25,868 --> 00:16:28,128
I just thought I'd check up on you.

253
00:16:29,448 --> 00:16:30,848
I'll walk you to the station.

254
00:16:31,168 --> 00:16:32,028
It's getting late.

255
00:16:32,348 --> 00:16:34,168
So you're not even gonna let me in?

256
00:16:34,448 --> 00:16:35,628
Well, that's impolite.

257
00:16:37,208 --> 00:16:38,108
Why not?

258
00:16:38,108 --> 00:16:42,428
I'm not ready.

259
00:16:42,768 --> 00:16:43,708
My place is a mess.

260
00:16:43,888 --> 00:16:44,528
So what?

261
00:16:44,968 --> 00:16:45,508
Show me.

262
00:16:46,268 --> 00:16:47,228
There's nothing to show.

263
00:16:47,308 --> 00:16:48,088
It's just a room.

264
00:16:49,328 --> 00:16:51,108
You're just full of lame excuses.

265
00:16:51,968 --> 00:16:54,308
If there's nothing to show, then it can't be messy.

266
00:16:55,488 --> 00:16:56,448
Look, forget it.

267
00:16:56,468 --> 00:16:57,768
The last train is about to...

268
00:16:57,768 --> 00:16:59,008
My feet are cold.

269
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:00,368
And I need the bathroom.

270
00:17:00,368 --> 00:17:03,288
Don't make me spell it out, you idiot!

271
00:17:10,248 --> 00:17:11,488
That's much better.

272
00:17:13,448 --> 00:17:15,488
Hey, how old is this place?

273
00:17:16,068 --> 00:17:19,208
It looks like a dump from the outside, but the inside's kind of nice.

274
00:17:20,328 --> 00:17:24,728
It's 26 years old, but the landlord renovated the interior recently.

275
00:17:28,448 --> 00:17:30,148
Well, aren't you the lucky one?

276
00:17:31,368 --> 00:17:32,288
Hey, Ray!

277
00:17:33,028 --> 00:17:34,148
Get me a towel.

278
00:17:39,448 --> 00:17:39,928
Thanks.

279
00:17:40,868 --> 00:17:43,148
Hey, why did you choose this town?

280
00:17:43,688 --> 00:17:46,168
It's not like you know anybody all the way out here.

281
00:17:46,668 --> 00:17:49,148
I had a job that sent me out here one time.

282
00:17:49,608 --> 00:17:51,208
I guess I liked it because of the river.

283
00:17:51,848 --> 00:17:52,428
The river?

284
00:17:53,168 --> 00:17:53,628
Really?

285
00:17:53,988 --> 00:17:56,148
I don't remember you liking rivers before.

286
00:17:56,148 --> 00:18:01,468
Hmm, the river, huh?

287
00:18:02,428 --> 00:18:07,988
We lived under the same roof for 10 years, but it seems like I don't know anything about you.

288
00:18:08,708 --> 00:18:10,528
Hey, it's getting cold in here.

289
00:18:10,808 --> 00:18:11,868
Can't you warm it up a little?

290
00:18:11,868 --> 00:18:12,868
Not really.

291
00:18:13,148 --> 00:18:15,048
I would, but the heater doesn't work that well.

292
00:18:15,208 --> 00:18:15,728
Hmm.

293
00:18:16,488 --> 00:18:17,568
The WAP!

294
00:18:17,788 --> 00:18:19,448
I didn't want you to open that!

295
00:18:19,888 --> 00:18:21,068
Wow, how fancy.

296
00:18:21,668 --> 00:18:23,388
This is a fine feather comforter.

297
00:18:23,788 --> 00:18:26,848
It was a gift from a friend of mine.

298
00:18:26,848 --> 00:18:32,008
Well, you must not have gotten it that long ago.

299
00:18:32,728 --> 00:18:34,408
It doesn't smell like you yet.

300
00:18:34,408 --> 00:18:45,028
Wow, you've got quite the view.

301
00:18:45,628 --> 00:18:47,208
This is only the sixth floor?

302
00:18:47,608 --> 00:18:48,908
It feels so high up.

303
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:50,268
Is it because the river's low?

304
00:18:52,408 --> 00:18:53,368
I see.

305
00:18:53,848 --> 00:18:55,548
So this is where you've been living.

306
00:18:57,128 --> 00:19:00,148
You looked for this place and decided all on your own.

307
00:19:01,048 --> 00:19:02,768
You're a pretty self-centered person.

308
00:19:02,768 --> 00:19:05,128
Dad was sad when you left.

309
00:19:05,748 --> 00:19:08,148
How'd you pull this off, being underage?

310
00:19:08,808 --> 00:19:09,908
Chairman Jinguji.

311
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:11,888
Oh, well that figures.

312
00:19:12,568 --> 00:19:14,648
He always did have a soft spot for you.

313
00:19:22,628 --> 00:19:23,928
Kyoko, the last train is...

314
00:19:23,928 --> 00:19:25,268
Why don't you go back home?

315
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:26,688
To that house.

316
00:19:27,388 --> 00:19:29,748
Dad would just be so happy to have you back.

317
00:19:32,768 --> 00:19:35,868
Hey, lend me a t-shirt for the night.

318
00:19:36,148 --> 00:19:37,008
I'm getting sleepy.

319
00:19:42,648 --> 00:19:44,648
Did you and father have a fight?

320
00:19:45,388 --> 00:19:46,268
Not at all.

321
00:19:46,868 --> 00:19:48,548
I mean, I haven't seen him.

322
00:19:49,088 --> 00:19:50,828
Actually, I haven't been home lately.

323
00:19:50,828 --> 00:19:55,808
Are you still with that guy?

324
00:20:04,268 --> 00:20:05,328
Thank goodness.

325
00:20:10,608 --> 00:20:12,468
At least it didn't leave a scar.

326
00:20:12,468 --> 00:20:21,888
Goto's not a decent person.

327
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:28,508
You should stay away from him.

328
00:20:29,448 --> 00:20:30,968
That's none of your business.

329
00:20:31,888 --> 00:20:33,628
Does he ever get violent with you?

330
00:20:34,548 --> 00:20:35,788
Violent? With me?

331
00:20:36,328 --> 00:20:37,108
As if.

332
00:20:37,108 --> 00:20:39,988
If he even dared to try and touch me.

333
00:20:40,388 --> 00:20:43,148
Do you really think I'd just stand there and take it?

334
00:20:45,408 --> 00:20:47,068
I'd stab him in his sleep.

335
00:20:47,628 --> 00:20:50,008
I'd make sure he'd never wake up again.

336
00:20:54,328 --> 00:20:55,348
You'd do that?

337
00:20:57,568 --> 00:20:58,048
Yeah.

338
00:20:59,148 --> 00:21:00,168
I love him.

339
00:21:00,168 --> 00:21:03,208
I truly love him.

340
00:21:18,888 --> 00:21:20,488
You couldn't sleep?

341
00:21:21,908 --> 00:21:23,428
Well, that's not good.

342
00:21:23,908 --> 00:21:25,908
Don't you have a rank deciding game today?

343
00:21:27,048 --> 00:21:28,448
Who's your opponent again?

344
00:21:30,168 --> 00:21:31,568
Oh, right.

345
00:21:31,908 --> 00:21:32,828
Mr. Matsunaga.

346
00:21:33,648 --> 00:21:34,708
How old is he?

347
00:21:36,928 --> 00:21:38,368
64 or 65?

348
00:21:39,008 --> 00:21:40,768
He's quite the fighter, isn't he?

349
00:21:41,188 --> 00:21:44,128
He won't move to the free class even after falling to C1.

350
00:21:44,528 --> 00:21:45,988
Just keeps hanging on desperately.

351
00:21:46,688 --> 00:21:47,228
Poor guy.

352
00:21:47,768 --> 00:21:49,608
I saw him play against dad once.

353
00:21:50,288 --> 00:21:52,568
It's like he was holding on for dear life.

354
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:53,708
Depressing.

355
00:21:54,548 --> 00:21:57,008
But he never quit even after all of that.

356
00:21:57,008 --> 00:21:59,908
He must love Shogi more than anything in the world.

357
00:22:00,748 --> 00:22:02,388
Unlike someone else I know.

358
00:22:05,528 --> 00:22:10,828
So, I hear that if Mr. Matsunaga is demoted from C1, he'll finally retire.

359
00:22:11,968 --> 00:22:13,068
That's too bad.

360
00:22:13,448 --> 00:22:17,148
It's like you're going over there to put an old, senile dog out of his misery.

361
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:18,928
I get it, though.

362
00:22:19,488 --> 00:22:22,088
Nobody wants to be the one to take out an old man.

363
00:22:22,088 --> 00:22:24,808
It kind of makes me worry, actually.

364
00:22:25,308 --> 00:22:30,068
I thought in a situation like this, maybe you'd be the kind of person who'd throw the match.

365
00:22:30,968 --> 00:22:31,488
Right.

366
00:22:31,908 --> 00:22:33,788
Since you're such a nice guy and all.

367
00:22:33,788 --> 00:22:45,888
As she walked away, the sun shined on her hair like liquid gold.

368
00:22:45,888 --> 00:22:55,688
But that light eventually brought on a pounding rainstorm.

369
00:22:55,688 --> 00:22:56,708
I hope you we win.

370
00:22:56,748 --> 00:22:57,608
I think I'm out of her hands.

371
00:22:57,608 --> 00:22:58,708
I haven't touched any of you.

372
00:22:58,708 --> 00:22:59,228
Oh, boy.

373
00:22:59,228 --> 00:23:00,628
Oh, boy.

374
00:23:00,628 --> 00:23:01,048
I think I'm just копie.

375
00:23:01,048 --> 00:23:05,868
If you want to have that moment, I want to take out a unity jegue moment.

376
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:39,011
Shouichi Matsunaga, 7th Den, 65 years old, from Fukushima.

377
00:24:39,011 --> 00:24:41,011
A pro at age 25.

378
00:24:41,011 --> 00:24:44,011
He's been playing the game for 40 years.

379
00:24:44,011 --> 00:24:46,011
I wonder how he feels right now.

380
00:24:46,011 --> 00:24:48,011
Ah, damn.

381
00:24:48,011 --> 00:24:51,011
It's time to start the match.

382
00:24:51,011 --> 00:24:55,011
Don't miss the next episode of March Comes In Like a Lion.

383
00:24:55,011 --> 00:24:58,011
Everyone needs a copy of Harunobu Nikaido's Shogi book.

384
00:24:58,011 --> 00:24:59,011
I insist.

385
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:04,011
We are also going through the stay tuned.

386
00:25:04,011 --> 00:25:07,011
I want to comment or comment what's possible I want to ask you.

387
00:25:17,011 --> 00:25:20,011
I want more.

388
00:25:20,011 --> 00:25:23,011
Remember afterBats come to aamoibo going through the day.

389
00:25:23,011 --> 00:25:28,011
There's no way for me.

